-       A `Git.Backend^{loggable, caps.any}` built as `Commandline(command)` from the
-       `Commandline.Command`, `WorkingDirectory`, `Environment` and `Commandline.Event is
-       Loggable` in scope: so import `gitCommands.searchpathGitCommand` (or bind a command),
-       `workingDirectories.javaBaseWorkingDirectory`, `environments.javaBaseEnvironment` and a
-       logging policy alongside it.
+   entry .commandlineGit   il backend che esegue il comando `git`
+       Un `Git.Backend^{loggable, caps.any}` costruito come `Commandline(command)` a partire da
+       `Commandline.Command`, `WorkingDirectory`, `Environment` e
+       `Commandline.Event is Loggable` nell'ambito: quindi si importano insieme a esso
+       `gitCommands.searchpathGitCommand` (o si lega un comando),
+       `workingDirectories.javaBaseWorkingDirectory`, `environments.javaBaseEnvironment` e una
+       politica di logging.

-   entry .soundnessGit   the native backend: reads and writes the repository's files itself, with no `git` binary
-       `Native()` with no transports, so it reaches repositories on the same filesystem by path
-       and raises `Git.Error(Unsupported(the transport for <url>))` for any other URL; a
-       program which fetches from or pushes to a remote over HTTP or SSH binds its own
-       `given Git.Backend = Native(List(SmartHttp(), SshCommand()))` instead. Imported by name,
-       since `import soundness.*` does not import givens; `gitBackends.commandlineGit` is the
-       alternative which runs the `git` command.
+   entry .soundnessGit   il backend nativo: legge e scrive da sé i file del repository, senza binario `git`
+       `Native()` senza trasporti, quindi raggiunge per percorso i repository sullo stesso
+       filesystem e solleva `Git.Error(Unsupported(the transport for <url>))` per qualsiasi
+       altro URL; un programma che fa fetch da un remote o push verso di esso tramite HTTP o SSH
+       lega invece il proprio `given Git.Backend = Native(List(SmartHttp(), SshCommand()))`.
+       Si importa per nome, poiché `import soundness.*` non importa i given;
+       `gitBackends.commandlineGit` è l'alternativa che esegue il comando `git`.

